<urn:atm:triage:finding/BB-READY-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB-READY-004" ;
  triage:title "prerelease.py's wait_for_archive times out before prerelease-archive.yml actually finishes, and polls too aggressively" ;
  triage:description "fenix (Phase BB closeout, 1.5.17 publish), found on integrate/phase-bb @ 5f2b1bb3d. .claude/skills/prerelease/scripts/prerelease.py::wait_for_archive (line ~330) bounds the prerelease-archive.yml wait at 60 x 5s = 5 min and polls `gh run list` every 5s. The 1.5.17 publish (tag prerelease/v1.5.17 @ 5f2b1bb3d) exited 'timed out waiting for prerelease-archive.yml for prerelease/v1.5.17' at ~5 min while run 34746170926 completed success at 7.5 min (the 1.5.16 run took 7.4 min) -- so --publish never ran its Release asset/checksum verification, and the 5s cadence spends 60 API calls per publish (budget rule is <=1 call per 10 min per object). fenix independently verified the assets by hand: checksums.txt matches both the host and linux-aarch64 tarballs." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "tooling" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "fenix, Phase BB closeout (1.5.17 publish)" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope ".claude/skills/prerelease/scripts/prerelease.py (wait_for_archive, line ~330)" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-13T07:58:19Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Lead ruling (2026-09-13, team-lead): important, not blocking -- fenix hand-verified the 1.5.17 release assets/checksums are correct, so this is a tooling gap (premature timeout, over-budget polling cadence) not a release-integrity defect. Phase BB closeout tooling, not tied to any BB.N sprint's deliverables; attributed foundIn to BB3 following the same bookkeeping-reuse pattern as BB-READY-003 (BB3's own sprint work and its BB-READY-003 fix are both closed/merged, freeing the slot). Proposed fix (fenix): wait up to 20 min, poll every 60s. Fix to be dispatched by fenix to cipher after the host smoke finishes." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB3 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-13T07:58:19Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/BB-READY-004/1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

